PART 2: WHAT IS BABEL?

================================================================================

Babel Definition

Babel is a JavaScript compiler/toolchain.

It can transform JavaScript syntax according to configured plugins, presets, and target environments.

Feature              | Description
---------------------|---------------------------------------------
Type                 | JavaScript compiler/toolchain
JSX                  | Can transform JSX syntax
Modern JavaScript    | Can transform newer JavaScript features
Plugins              | Perform individual transformations
Presets              | Group related plugins/configuration
Open Source          | Open-source project
Build Integration    | Can be integrated into frontend build tooling

Simplified Babel Flow

Using the classic JSX transform as an example:

JSX

<h1>Hello World</h1>

        ↓

BABEL / JSX TRANSFORM

        ↓

JavaScript

React.createElement(
  'h1',
  null,
  'Hello World'
)

        ↓

React processes the element


Important: React.createElement() represents the classic JSX transform. Modern React can use the automatic JSX runtime, where the generated JavaScript may use functions such as jsx() / jsxs() instead.

================================================================================

WHY IS A JSX TRANSFORM NEEDED?

================================================================================

JSX:

const element = <h1>Hello World</h1>;


The JSX syntax must be transformed before normal JavaScript execution.

Classic transformation:

const element =
  React.createElement(
    'h1',
    null,
    'Hello World'
  );


Easy memory:

JSX
 ↓
TRANSFORM
 ↓
JAVASCRIPT
 ↓
REACT ELEMENT


