PART 5: UNDERSTANDING React.createElement()

================================================================================

Syntax
React.createElement(
  type,
  props,
  ...children
);

Parameters
Parameter    | Typical Value        | Description
-------------|----------------------|----------------------------------
type         | string/component     | HTML tag or React component
props        | object/null          | Element properties
...children  | renderable values    | Child content/elements

Example
React.createElement(
  'h1',
  {
    className: 'title'
  },
  'Hello World'
);


Conceptually represents:

<h1 className="title">
  Hello World
</h1>


================================================================================

React.createElement() RETURN VALUE

================================================================================

React.createElement() returns a React element, not an actual browser DOM element.

Conceptually, a React element contains information such as:

{
  type: 'h1',

  props: {
    className: 'title',
    children: 'Hello World'
  },

  key: null
}


React element implementations can contain additional internal fields. Those internal fields should not be treated as application APIs.

Important Properties
Property   | Purpose
-----------|-----------------------------------------------
type       | Element/component type
props      | Properties and children
key        | Helps React identify list elements
ref        | Used by React's ref mechanism when applicable

Important Difference
React Element
     ↓
JavaScript Description of UI

NOT

Actual Browser DOM Element


