PART 6: BABEL CONFIGURATION

================================================================================

Babel configuration determines which transformations are applied.

Common configuration files include:

.babelrc
babel.config.js

Example Configuration
{
  "presets": [
    [
      "@babel/preset-react",
      {
        "runtime": "automatic"
      }
    ],
    "@babel/preset-env"
  ]
}

Explanation
Configuration             | Purpose
--------------------------|--------------------------------------------
@babel/preset-react       | Configures React/JSX transformations
@babel/preset-env         | Transforms JS according to target setup
runtime: "automatic"      | Uses the automatic JSX runtime

Important Automatic Runtime Detail

With:

{
  "runtime": "automatic"
}


JSX does not necessarily compile to React.createElement().

Modern JSX transformation can automatically use JSX runtime functions instead.

Therefore:

Classic Runtime
JSX
 ↓
React.createElement()


Automatic Runtime
JSX
 ↓
JSX Runtime Functions


This is why a manual:

import React from 'react';


is not required solely for JSX in many modern React setups.

================================================================================

BABEL PRESETS

================================================================================

What is a Preset?

A Babel preset is a preconfigured collection of Babel transformations/plugins intended for a particular use case.

Preset                    | Purpose
--------------------------|----------------------------------
@babel/preset-react       | React / JSX transformation
@babel/preset-env         | Modern JavaScript transformation
@babel/preset-typescript  | TypeScript syntax transformation


Easy memory:

PLUGIN
→ Specific Transformation


PRESET
→ Collection / Configuration of Transformations


