PART 7: BABEL IN A REACT PROJECT

================================================================================

React Tooling

Different React toolchains can handle JSX transformation differently.

A project may use:

Tool / Layer          | Role
----------------------|--------------------------------------------
Babel                 | JavaScript/JSX transformations
Vite                  | Development/build tooling
React Plugin          | React integration with build tool
Bundler/Build System  | Produces application assets

Vite Configuration Example
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    react()
  ]
});


The important idea is:

React Source Code
      ↓
Vite / React Plugin
      ↓
JSX + React Processing
      ↓
Development / Production Output


The exact transformation pipeline depends on the Vite/plugin version and configuration, so it is better not to assume that every Vite React project translates every JSX expression through Babel into classic React.createElement() calls.

