================================================================================

CLASSIC VS AUTOMATIC JSX RUNTIME

================================================================================

Classic JSX Runtime              | Automatic JSX Runtime
---------------------------------|----------------------------------------
React.createElement()            | JSX runtime functions
Historically required React      | JSX alone doesn't require React import
import for JSX compilation       | solely for JSX
Older teaching examples          | Common modern React tooling

Important Interview Point

If asked:

"Does Babel always convert JSX into React.createElement()?"

Answer:

No. The classic JSX transform produces React.createElement() calls, while modern React tooling can use the automatic JSX runtime and generate JSX-runtime function calls instead.

